Z||000000||JohnnyK||08-06-2000||03:08 AM||||Has anyone ever attempted to put an air intake on the right side of the car that would blow air right into the engine compartment? I don't like how hot it gets in there (too hot to touch the plug wires, let alone anything else, is that normal?) and think it would be a great idea to get some air blowing through there. I was thinking of making it look exactly like the left side intake? Possible?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||08-06-2000||09:54 AM||||theres a hole on the right side like the one on the left. its got insulation over it. if you got some of the side scoops or integrated rocker panels various venders sell you could take advantage of it.<P>i thought i read or heard once that scoops or intakes on each side were the original plan, but got nixed (cost cutting?), and only a few '88's eventually got them. i've seen them (actually just one), but i had though it was something the owner added on.<P>i've got side scoops but beyond opening up the right side hole (just made a hole in the insulation) i haven't tried to make use of them yet.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-06-2000||10:47 AM||||ive got a Ferrari kit on mine, it has a scoop on both sides, i got the left one ducted to air filter, right one is ducted to an opening under all the trash insulation under the battery. blows rite in front and backside of engine. I even thought of adding a small 12v fan in duct from a RV shop thats used in the furnace duct, its only like 3X5 inches.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-06-2000).]||||reg||1
